    "result_text": "All 26 tests pass (BUILD SUCCESS).\n\n## Summary\n\nI changed the customerCode format from `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` to `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` with a per-city sequence.\n\n**`ClinicServiceImpl.generateCustomerCode`** (`src/main/java/.../service/ClinicServiceImpl.java:262`):\n- Prepends `CITY3` \u2014 the upper-cased first three letters of the owner's city.\n- Changed `NNNN` from a **global** owner count to a **per-city** sequence: one more than the number of existing owners whose city matches (case-insensitively). Two owners in the same city now get consecutive numbers.\n- Updated the Javadoc to describe the new format.\n\n**Membership number** \u2014 I confirmed nothing else needed code changes. `OwnerMapper.membershipNumber` builds `<customerCode>-M<YY>` by concatenating whatever `getCustomerCode()` returns, so it automatically rebuilds on the new format. I only refreshed the stale example in its Javadoc (`SMI-0007-M26` \u2192 `LON-SMI-0007-M26`).\n\nI also verified there's no seed data in the SQL files carrying hardcoded customer codes (the `customer_code` column is defined in schema, but `data.sql` doesn't populate it).\n\nEverything is green: the three target tests (Cp09 per-city sequence, Cp14 membership number, Cp16 city-prefix format) and the full 26-test suite pass.",
